{# Widget "map" — presence on the area's stations layer.

   THE PREVIEW IS THE WIDGET, so this draws the real plate on the dashboard
   and in the library alike, from the same live answer the Live tab reads.
   A picture of a map in the library and a map on the dashboard would be two
   things that drift.

   THE GROUND IS THE AREA'S AND THE MARKERS ARE THIS MODULE'S. The boundary,
   the zones, the posts, the imagery, the controls and the key belong to
   whoever owns them; the roster contributes one point layer per presence
   state and the legend group over them, and draws nothing itself.

   A CARD NEVER GROWS WITH ITS DATA, so the plate is a FIXED height — the
   same rule that bounds a list to latest-N and a calendar cell to its
   pills. A map that grew with the park would own the dashboard. #}
<div class="c">
    <span class="tab">Presence on the stations layer<span class="src">&middot; {{ dash.live.positions }} position{{ dash.live.positions == 1 ? '' : 's' }} &middot; {{ dash.live.stale }} stale &middot; {{ dash.live.withoutAFix }} with none</span></span>
    <a class="more" href="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterController::LIVE_ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">The live plate &rarr;</a>

    {{ render_map(dash.plate, {'--map-plate-height': '320px'}) }}
</div>
